---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: sage-experience-page
  namespace: documentation
data:
  index.html: |
    <!doctype html>
    <html lang="en">
      <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
        <title>Kalaxy3 / SAGE — Governed outcome</title>
        <style>
          body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 900px; margin: 3rem auto; padding: 0 1.25rem; line-height: 1.55; }
          .ok { font-weight: 700; }
          section { margin: 2rem 0; }
        </style>
      </head>
      <body>
        <h1>Kalaxy3 / SAGE governed outcome</h1>
        <p class="ok">Authenticated origin path: serving from the Kalaxy3 Kubernetes cluster.</p>
        <section>
          <h2>What was requested</h2>
          <p>Prove an Architect-intent-to-runtime-outcome lifecycle with governed LLM contribution, a real cluster capability, zero-trust external access, measurable verification, evidence, and promotion back to main.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>What SAGE challenged</h2>
          <p>Anonymous publication was rejected by the Architect. Human external access requires Cloudflare Access MFA; privileged management surfaces remain private.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>What changed</h2>
          <p>The experience reuses the existing Kalaxy3 documentation image and Traefik ingress. Cloudflare Tunnel is the outbound external transport; Access supplies the external identity boundary.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>What SAGE prevented</h2>
          <p>The Architect explicitly stated that installing Cloudflare into Kubernetes should be SAGE's engineering burden rather than operator knowledge. SAGE first found that the encrypted Vault source could not be decrypted from the root deployment entry point. After that correction, the first real deployment stopped again before cluster mutation because inherited Ansible privilege-escalation state overrode the intended controller-local boundary. SAGE preserved secret redaction, corrected the precedence boundary, and did not ask the Architect to bypass the governed path.</p>
          <p>The Architect then clarified the workload semantics: cloudflared is a platform service, node-level HA outranks ordinary placement preference, amd64-01 capacity should be preserved for AI when alternatives exist, and ARM64 capacity must not be ignored. SAGE converts that into hard cross-node separation plus soft placement preferences instead of a brittle node-name rule.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Health and evidence</h2>
          <p>If this page is visible after Access authentication, the protected external request reached the live cluster-hosted origin. Deterministic workload, tunnel, routing, and negative-access evidence is recorded separately by SAGE.</p>
          <p><a href="/evidence/">Browse evidence</a> · <a href="/standards/kalaxy3-sage-operating-contract/">SAGE operating contract</a></p>
        </section>
      </body>
    </html>
  healthz: |
    ok
---
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: sage-experience
  namespace: documentation
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app.kubernetes.io/name: sage-experience
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app.kubernetes.io/name: sage-experience
    spec:
      automountServiceAccountToken: false
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: "{{ sage_experience_image_ref }}"
          imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
          ports:
            - name: http
              containerPort: 80
          volumeMounts:
            - name: landing
              mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html
              subPath: index.html
              readOnly: true
            - name: landing
              mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html/healthz
              subPath: healthz
              readOnly: true
          readinessProbe:
            httpGet:
              path: /healthz
              port: http
            initialDelaySeconds: 3
            periodSeconds: 10
          livenessProbe:
            httpGet:
              path: /healthz
              port: http
            initialDelaySeconds: 10
            periodSeconds: 20
          securityContext:
            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
      volumes:
        - name: landing
          configMap:
            name: sage-experience-page
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: sage-experience
  namespace: documentation
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: sage-experience
  ports:
    - name: http
      port: 80
      targetPort: http
---
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress
metadata:
  name: sage-experience
  namespace: documentation
  annotations:
    traefik.ingress.kubernetes.io/router.entrypoints: web
spec:
  rules:
    - host: {{ sage_external_hostname }}
      http:
        paths:
          - path: /
            pathType: Prefix
            backend:
              service:
                name: sage-experience
                port:
                  name: http
